# Copy this file to .env in the repo root and fill it in. Never put real values in this file,
# and never commit the .env. SETUP.md walks through every variable.
#
# Paths in here should be absolute. The agent starts the server from its own working directory,
# so relative paths resolve against the consuming project, not this repo.

# Entra ID tenant of the assistant account. `az account show --query tenantId -o tsv`, or the
# Entra portal overview page.
TEAMS_MCP_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# The dedicated assistant account. One account per consuming project — see SETUP.md step 1.
TEAMS_MCP_USERNAME=
# Single-quote the password. Node strips the quotes and takes the content literally; a shell
# sourcing the file does the same. A quote character inside the value ends it early, so a
# password containing a single quote goes in double quotes instead.
TEAMS_MCP_PASSWORD=''

# Which of Microsoft's first-party client ids to sign in as. Both need no app registration and
# no admin consent. Unset, the server uses the Teams first-party client id (the
# TEAMS_FIRST_PARTY_CLIENT_ID constant in src/config.ts), which authenticates everywhere but on
# some tenants returns a token with no chat scopes at all — every /chats call then fails 403.
# The Microsoft Office first-party client id returned a fully scoped token on the tenant this
# was developed against and is the recommended value. Microsoft publishes the application ids of
# its own first-party apps; look up "Microsoft Office" in that list and put the id here.
TEAMS_MCP_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_CLIENT_ID

# Allowlist config. Required — the server will not start without it. Absolute path.
TEAMS_MCP_CONFIG=/absolute/path/to/teams-assistant-mcp/teams-mcp.config.json

# Where the refresh token is cached (written 0600). Absolute path into this repo, where the
# name is gitignored; the default lands in the agent's working directory instead. The @mention
# member cache (.members-cache.json) is written next to this file, same directory.
TEAMS_MCP_TOKEN_CACHE=/absolute/path/to/teams-assistant-mcp/.token-cache.json

# How long a chat's cached member list (used to resolve @mentions) is trusted before a refresh.
# Defaults to 24h (86400 seconds); chat membership in a fixed allowlist rarely changes.
# TEAMS_MCP_MEMBERS_TTL_SECONDS=86400

# Where get_chat_attachment writes downloaded files. Defaults to a directory under the OS
# tmpdir, which the OS may clean between sessions — set this if downloads should stick around.
# TEAMS_MCP_DOWNLOAD_DIR=/absolute/path/to/teams-assistant-mcp/downloads

# OneDrive folder (under the assistant account's drive root) where send_chat_file parks uploads
# before sharing them into the chat. Created on first upload.
# TEAMS_MCP_UPLOAD_DIR=ai-test

# Overrides the display name `npm run probe` checks the account against. Defaults to
# "Assistant (AI)"; set it to the account's real display name.
# TEAMS_MCP_DISPLAY_NAME=

# Where the background inbox poller appends new messages, one JSON line each. Defaults to
# ~/.teams-assistant/inbox.jsonl; the watermark sidecar (inbox-state.json) lives next to it.
# TEAMS_INBOX_PATH=

# Set to 1 to not run the background inbox poller at all (for consumers that only post).
# TEAMS_INBOX_DISABLED=1
